{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1533938-issue-with-first-change-story","id":1533938,"title":"Issue with First Change Story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-10T00:17:01-07:00","id":1533938,"title":"Issue with First Change Story","content":"I recently re-read the Werewolf corebook and wanted to play a short story about bunch of Wolf-Blooded teenagers going through their First Change - preferably while meeting with supernatural threat from Werewolf universe face-to-face, for example Urged. But I ran into problem. Since First Change is tied to the phase of moon under which First Change happened, I have only two choices:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spread out First Changes over the story (which would necessarily make it long enough to fit all them in, narratively speaking);</li> <li>Do them all at once, but then resulting pack are all of one Auspice, which really cripples the pack and chances of taking this short story and making it into full Werewolf game.</li> </ol>Did anyone else had that problem in their First Change Story? Any advice on what to do? I really want to keep this to one, maybe two sessions of game, but at the same time, would like to give myself a chance to evolve this game into something more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T04:29:39-07:00","id":1533951,"title":"","content":"While a big forced, since getting all five moons only takes 2 weeks, I was once is a game that took advantage of the nuzusul period. Basically the short intro story (we just had mortals, no wolf-blooded, doesn't really change anything) kicked us all into being nuzusul, but the antagonist traveled long distances on a regular schedule (local-ish week long cruises). So, in real time, we could very quickly hand wave two weeks away as we figured out the prey's schedule and could only prepare while waiting for it to come around again (missing the first chance by not knowing about it yet), and thus we all changed on our moons during that period.<br /> <br /> So it's basically the first option, but with a narrative that allowed for a long enough down time to have a rushed-but-plausible period for the changes to happen and every Auspice represented.<br /> <br /> That said, IME the game doesn't break if you have an uneven (or even all the same) Auspices (having an Ithaeur, Elodoth, and Cahalith mix can drastically reduce the amount of narrative time needed for changes to happen). There's no Auspice only mechanics that are so vital that if you don't have one of each the game can't go on for longer play. The bigger concern is how much the players will react to having an &quot;imbalanced&quot; party where they can all do a few things in-common, and there's a few things none of them can do. Some people aren't bothered by that (esp. with Tribes to help differentiate characters more), some are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T14:13:26-07:00","id":1534000,"title":"","content":"It may be a bit overboard for what you're envisioning for the story, but you could invoke Storyteller-fiat to say some cosmic hullabaloo allows for multiple auspices to Change at once. Like maybe the moon counts as being in all phases during a solar eclipse, because reasons. Or maybe each character gets possessed by an appropriate Lune, causing a pseudo-Change that isn't actually official until the next appropriate moon phase. Just throwing out ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}